        <title>A quantitative central limit theorem for Poisson horospheres in high dimensions</title>
        <authors>Zakhar Kabluchko, Daniel Rosen, Christoph Th\&#34;ale</authors>
        <categories>math.PR math.MG</categories>
            <comments>10 pages, 1 figure</comments>
            <msc-class>52A55, 60D05 (Primary), 60F05, 60G55 (Secondary)</msc-class>
            <license>http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/</license>
            <abstract>Consider a stationary Poisson process of horospheres in a $d$-dimensional hyperbolic space. In the focus of this note is the total surface area these random horospheres induce in a sequence of balls of growing radius $R$. The main result is a quantitative, non-standard central limit theorem for these random variables as the radius $R$ of the balls and the space dimension $d$ tend to infinity simultaneously.</abstract>
